oeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782063093525039001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2a8bff2d-0245-49ee-8361-ef8ec58388b3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5fd2-a7c2-0aec-48fa"},{"link_uuid":"f8d5ac9c-b4e9-429a-80c9-3d82d314292c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"86ac-086a-20ad-4327"}],"description":"## Context\nThe plan-review gate (`5fd2`) deliberately EXEMPTS bugs in v1 — a bug has a different shape (reproduction,\nexpected-vs-actual, fix-plan) than a feature plan, and round-4 data showed the plan criteria draw mostly\nplanning-noise on bugs. This epic designs the dedicated bug-review gate. (Spun out of `5fd2`; was follow-on F6.)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A bug-specific criteria set (reproduction, expected-vs-actual, root-cause, regression test) on the three-pass structure.\n- [ ] Validated on real bug tickets across the corpuses; low false-positive vs the plan criteria on bugs.\n- [ ] Reuses the shared review infrastructure (engine, Pass-2/Pass-3, eval seam).\n- [ ] A review gate tuned to bug tickets (reproduction adequacy, root-cause vs symptom, fix-plan soundness,\n- [ ] Bugs are no longer simply skipped: they get an appropriate, low-false-positive review.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"reconciler","managed_refs":[["relates_to","5fd2-a7c2-0aec-48fa"],["relates_to","86ac-086a-20ad-4327"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"556db391-c3e4-4550-9348-cf5831e4b02b","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3e50-4905-7830-432f","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Bug-ticket review gate (dedicated; the plan-review gate exempts bugs in v1)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["72071429-1